Filed this afternoon. Copy attached.<br />
<br />
The opposition runs on three points and the documents carry all three. The =
2011 examination did not close with no findings; it closed on a written und=
ertaking, and the undertaking is in the record in the registrant's own word=
s. The undertaking had no expiration and by its terms reached accounts acqu=
ired later, so the conduct charged from 2019 forward is a breach of it rath=
er than a continuation of something the staff blessed. And Respondent's own=
 conduct in 2013 shows the firm understood the undertaking to bind it, beca=
use it applied the undertaking to the Hollis Grange accounts unprompted and=
 paid for a surprise examination it now says it was never required to obtai=
n.<br />
<br />
On the fee application, the answer is the production itself. A position sup=
ported by the respondent's own signed undertaking is substantially justifie=
d.<br />
<br />
One point I want flagged internally rather than in the filing. Respondent's=
 motion was not frivolous when it was made. The examination file the Divisi=
on produced in May really did contain nothing but a summary record and a cl=
osing letter, and that is our doing, not theirs. Counsel drew the only infe=
rence that record supported.<br />
<br />
Terrence
